### Accessory Service API Tests
### Use with REST Client VS Code extension

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8030

### ============================================
### Health Check Endpoints
### ============================================

### Root endpoint - Service info
GET {{baseUrl}}/ HTTP/1.1

###

### Health check - Database connectivity
GET {{baseUrl}}/health HTTP/1.1

### ============================================
### Create Accessories
### ============================================

### Create a toy accessory
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Interactive Ball",
    "type": "toy",
    "price": 15.99,
    "stock": 25,
    "size": "L",
    "imageUrl": "https://example.com/ball.jpg",
    "description": "LED light-up ball that keeps pets entertained for hours"
}

###

### Create a food accessory (low stock)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Premium Kibble",
    "type": "food",
    "price": 29.99,
    "stock": 8,
    "size": "M",
    "imageUrl": "https://example.com/kibble.jpg",
    "description": "High-quality dry food with natural ingredients"
}

###

### Create a collar accessory
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "LED Safety Collar",
    "type": "collar",
    "price": 22.50,
    "stock": 15,
    "size": "M",
    "imageUrl": "https://example.com/collar.jpg",
    "description": "Rechargeable LED collar for nighttime visibility"
}

###

### Create a bedding accessory (low stock)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Memory Foam Bed",
    "type": "bedding",
    "price": 49.99,
    "stock": 5,
    "size": "XL",
    "imageUrl": "https://example.com/bed.jpg",
    "description": "Orthopedic memory foam bed for senior pets"
}

###

### Create a grooming accessory
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Slicker Brush",
    "type": "grooming",
    "price": 18.99,
    "stock": 12,
    "size": "M",
    "description": "Professional grooming brush for all coat types"
}

### ============================================
### Get Accessories (List & Filter)
### ============================================

### Get all accessories
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories HTTP/1.1

###

### Get accessories with pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories?limit=5&offset=0 HTTP/1.1

###

### Search accessories by name
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories?search=ball HTTP/1.1

###

### Search in descriptions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories?search=LED HTTP/1.1

###

### Filter by type (toy)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories?type=toy HTTP/1.1

###

### Filter by type (food)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories?type=food HTTP/1.1

###

### Get low stock items only
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories?lowStockOnly=true HTTP/1.1

###

### Combined filters - food items with low stock
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories?type=food&lowStockOnly=true HTTP/1.1

### ============================================
### Get Single Accessory
### ============================================

### Get seeded toy accessory
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories/seed-toy-001 HTTP/1.1

###

### Get seeded food accessory (low stock)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories/seed-food-001 HTTP/1.1

###

### Get non-existent accessory (should return 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories/non-existent-id HTTP/1.1

### ============================================
### Update Accessories
### ============================================

### Update stock only
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories/seed-toy-001 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "stock": 100
}

###

### Update price and description
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories/seed-food-001 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "price": 39.99,
    "description": "Updated: Premium organic dry food for adult dogs"
}

###

### Update multiple fields
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories/seed-toy-001 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Super Squeaky Ball",
    "price": 14.99,
    "stock": 75,
    "size": "L"
}

### ============================================
### Delete Accessories
### ============================================

### Delete seeded toy (use with caution)
# DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories/seed-toy-001 HTTP/1.1

###

### Delete non-existent accessory (should return 404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories/non-existent-id HTTP/1.1

### ============================================
### Validation Tests (Expected Errors)
### ============================================

### Invalid type (should return 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Invalid Item",
    "type": "furniture",
    "price": 10.00,
    "stock": 5,
    "size": "M"
}

###

### Negative price (should return 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Negative Price Item",
    "type": "toy",
    "price": -5.00,
    "stock": 10,
    "size": "S"
}

###

### Missing required fields (should return 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Incomplete Item",
    "price": 15.99
}

###

### Invalid size (should return 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Invalid Size Item",
    "type": "toy",
    "price": 10.00,
    "stock": 5,
    "size": "XXL"
}

###

### Name too long (should return 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/accessories HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "This name is way too long and exceeds the maximum allowed length of 200 characters which should trigger a validation error from the Pydantic model because we have set a max_length constraint on this field to prevent excessively long names from being stored in the database",
    "type": "toy",
    "price": 10.00,
    "stock": 5,
    "size": "M"
}
